<Ui xmlns="http://www.blizzard.com/wow/ui/" xmlns:xsi="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema-instance"
    xsi:schemaLocation="http://www.blizzard.com/wow/ui/ https://raw.githubusercontent.com/Gethe/wow-ui-source/live/Interface/FrameXML/UI_shared.xsd">
    <!--! WotLK fix: Cell uses native 3.3.5 Frame backdrop methods directly; no
         BackdropTemplate inheritance is required by the active widget graph.
         2026-08-08: loading of this very file aborted in the P0-B1 run because
         Widgets_IndicatorSettings.lua called the raw global GetClassColor, which
         3.3.5 does not have and an external addon had been supplying. That call
         now uses F.GetClassColor / F.GetClassColorStr (GAP-015).
         2026-08-11: the no-consumer claim above is now machine-checked, not
         grepped - the GAP-015 site read "SecureUnitButtonTemplate,BackDropTemplate",
         a comma list in a different letter case, which a plain grep for the
         published name misses. Run `python audit/tools/dormant_check.py`: it
         splits template lists, compares case-insensitively, and reports
         BackdropTemplate dead across every consumption channel. -->
    <Script file="Animation.lua"/>
    <Script file="Widgets.lua"/>
    <Script file="Widgets_IndicatorSettings.lua"/>
    <Script file="ColorPicker.lua"/>
    <Include file="TooltipTemplate_Classic.xml"/>
    <Script file="Tooltip.lua"/>
</Ui>